# Lien Project Rules

`CLAUDE.md` at the repo root is the single source of truth for project
structure, discovery policy, and commit gates — read it. This file is
deliberately thin: a duplicated package tree or gate list drifts out of sync
the moment either side changes (as this file previously did for months).

**Load-bearing facts, kept minimal on purpose:**
- Packages: `parser` ← `cli` (published as `@liendev/parser` /
  `@liendev/lien`, alongside `@liendev/parser-native`); `site` is private and
  unpublished. `core`, `review` and `action` have all been deleted.
- Nothing is stored. There is no index, no database and no search — Lien
  parses the working tree on demand and answers from that.
- The surface is four commands: `lien complexity`, `lien health`,
  `lien review`, `lien delta`.
- Before every commit, no exceptions: `npm run format:check`, `npm run lint`,
  `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `npm test`, `lien delta`, and
  `node .github/scripts/docs-truth.mjs`.
- Commits follow Conventional Commits (`feat(scope): ...`, `fix(scope): ...`);
  never `git commit --amend`.
